{"reference":"Genesis 21","book":"Genesis","chapter":21,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The ancestral movement","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Genesis moves from universal origins in chapters 1–11 to ancestral family narratives in chapters 12–50, ending with Jacob's household in Egypt. Genesis 21 is part of that ancestral family movement and contributes to the larger story that follows the opening chapters.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_021_7a36f6e82f34df18a8916a2d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
